---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import MediaFigure from '../../components/MediaFigure.astro';
import { ASSETS } from '../../data/assets';
import { MAP_REGIONS } from '../../data/gear';
import { CHAPTERS } from '../../data/chapter-guide';

const title = 'Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy Maps';
const description =
  'Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy maps and regions: the Venice lagoon camp, Venice and its carnival, the Minotaur’s Island across two eras, and where each chapter takes place.';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Maps', url: '/maps/' },
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} pageType="collection" breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <div class="container py-10">
    <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} />
    <header class="mt-6 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="section-kicker">World</p>
      <h1 class="section-title">Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy maps</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-fog">
        Two eras, one island, plus Venice. Use this as a region list, then open the chapter walkthrough
        for the route inside each space.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="mt-8"><MediaFigure {...ASSETS.islandOverlook} /></div>

    <div class="prose-page mt-10 max-w-3xl">
      <h2>Is there an open map?</h2>
      <p>
        No. Steam reviewers describe the story as linear, and the game is split into {CHAPTERS.length} chapters
        rather than one open world. Exploration means side rooms, dead-end ledges and alternate corners inside each
        area, not free travel between regions. If you miss something, the way back is a chapter replay through{' '}
        <a href="/story-select-cleanup/">Story Select</a>, not a fast-travel point.
      </p>

      <h2>Two time periods</h2>
      <p>
        Sophia’s half of the story is set in the early 14th century, about 15 years before A Plague Tale: Requiem.
        The other half takes place in the Minoan civilisation around 2000 BC, through Theseus’s memories. Several
        locations are the same stone in both eras, which is why the island regions below are marked “both eras”.
      </p>

      <h2>The Venice lagoon camp</h2>
      <p>
        The game opens in a plunderers’ camp in the lagoons near Venice, where Sophia grew up under her father
        Alec. Asobo’s DEVBLOG #3 says it was built out from the Red City Arena in Requiem, with worn fabrics and
        hanging cloth added, and that the team looked at wooden working-class districts in Africa and Asia because
        14th-century references for such a settlement barely exist.
      </p>

      <h2>Venice and the carnival</h2>
      <p>
        Venice is still largely preserved from the era, so the architecture was the easy part. The hard part,
        according to the developers, was the carnival and its huge crowds. The carnival is in Chapter 2, Felons,
        where watching the full puppet show unlocks the Theater enthusiast achievement.
      </p>

      <h2>The island and its references</h2>
      <p>
        Most of the game happens on the legendary island, hidden somewhere in the Mediterranean. To avoid
        repetition the team pulled references from across Greece:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The Cyclades</strong> — white limestone cliffs, turquoise water and pine, the baseline look.</li>
        <li><strong>Santorini and Stromboli</strong> — volcanic landscapes and darker rock.</li>
        <li><strong>Thiorichio</strong> — more colourful rock formations.</li>
        <li><strong>Preveli Beach</strong> — varied vegetation.</li>
        <li><strong>Knossos and Akrotiri</strong> — the Minoan architecture itself.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Core Minoan elements such as columns and friezes were kept, then blended with later Greek and Roman
        influences so the large arenas read as coherent. Full background is on the{' '}
        <a href="/locations/">locations and world guide</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Named areas from the walkthrough</h2>
      <p>
        Inside the island chapters, the guides on this site point to these named sections and arenas: “The
        Architect” in <a href="/walkthrough/chapter-6-what-lies-beneath/">Chapter 6</a>, the Black Temple arena
        and “The Whole Damn Army” in <a href="/walkthrough/chapter-7-death-it-sowed/">Chapter 7</a>, the palace,
        its petrified area and “Hunted” in <a href="/walkthrough/chapter-9-night-has-come/">Chapter 9</a>, the
        mine exit in <a href="/walkthrough/chapter-11-patera/">Chapter 11</a>, and the heart of the Labyrinth with
        the Minotaur statue in <a href="/walkthrough/chapter-13-as-one/">Chapter 13</a>. The eight Blades are in
        the Heroes’ Graves — bull-pillar crypts off the main route.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      {
        MAP_REGIONS.map((r) => (
          <li class="surface overflow-hidden p-0">
            <img src={r.image} alt={r.imageAlt} width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-44 w-full object-cover" />
            <div class="p-5">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-bone">{r.name}</h2>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-wheat">{r.era}</p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-fog">{r.note}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-black text-bone">Chapters on the map</h2>
    <ol class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-fog">
      {
        CHAPTERS.map((ch) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/walkthrough/${ch.slug}/`} class="font-bold text-wheat underline-offset-2 hover:underline">
              Chapter {ch.number}: {ch.title}
            </a>
            <span class="text-fog"> — {ch.setting}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>
</Layout>
